-- en: "Check whether you or your pet know this exact spell ID. An unlearned spell is a valid condition that returns false, so the same rotation can adapt as you learn abilities. This does not check cooldown, resources, range, or whether the spell can currently be cast. Missing or restricted learned-state data stays unavailable under NOT."
L["Check whether you or your pet know this exact spell ID. An unlearned spell is a valid condition that returns false, so the same rotation can adapt as you learn abilities. This does not check cooldown, resources, range, or whether the spell can currently be cast. Missing or restricted learned-state data stays unavailable under NOT."] = "Comprueba si tú o tu mascota conocéis este ID de hechizo exacto. Un hechizo no aprendido es una condición válida que devuelve falso, así que la misma rotación puede adaptarse a medida que aprendes habilidades. No comprueba el tiempo de reutilización, los recursos, el alcance ni si el hechizo se puede lanzar en este momento. Los datos de aprendizaje que faltan o están restringidos siguen sin estar disponibles bajo NO."
-- en: "Only consider auras that you applied yourself."
L["Only consider auras that you applied yourself."] = "Considera solo las auras que hayas aplicado tú."
-- en: "Remaining aura time is measured in seconds. Permanent auras have no expiration and do not satisfy a finite refresh threshold. An absent aura does not satisfy this condition. Restricted or unknown timing is unavailable, including under NOT."
L["Remaining aura time is measured in seconds. Permanent auras have no expiration and do not satisfy a finite refresh threshold. An absent aura does not satisfy this condition. Restricted or unknown timing is unavailable, including under NOT."] = "El tiempo restante del aura se mide en segundos. Las auras permanentes no caducan y no cumplen un umbral de renovación finito. Un aura ausente no cumple esta condición. Un tiempo restringido o desconocido no está disponible, también bajo NO."
-- en: "Compare the application count of a matching aura, including charges such as Earth Shield. An absent aura does not satisfy this condition; an unreadable count is unavailable."
L["Compare the application count of a matching aura, including charges such as Earth Shield. An absent aura does not satisfy this condition; an unreadable count is unavailable."] = "Compara el número de aplicaciones de un aura coincidente, incluidas cargas como las de Escudo de tierra. Un aura ausente no cumple esta condición; un recuento ilegible no está disponible."
-- en: "Only consider debuffs returned by the game's dispellable aura filter. This does not guarantee your dispel is ready or in range."
L["Only consider debuffs returned by the game's dispellable aura filter. This does not guarantee your dispel is ready or in range."] = "Considera solo los perjuicios que devuelve el filtro de auras disipables del juego. No garantiza que tu disipación esté lista o al alcance."
-- en: "Unavailable conditions or unsupported data"
L["Unavailable conditions or unsupported data"] = "Condiciones no disponibles o datos no compatibles"
-- en: "Automatic switching tries nothing else, then the fallback (%s): no enabled rotation here can be selected now."
L["Automatic switching tries nothing else, then the fallback (%s): no enabled rotation here can be selected now."] = "El cambio automático no prueba nada más y pasa a la rotación de reserva (%s): ninguna rotación activada aquí se puede seleccionar ahora."
-- en: "Automatic switching tries the enabled rotations in priority order, yours and Built Ins alike: higher numbers are tried first, equal priorities by name. It picks the first that matches; a rotation with no switch condition always matches, so turn it off to keep it from being chosen. The fallback (Default) is used only when none matches. The rotation list is sorted in this same order and shows each priority."
L["Automatic switching tries the enabled rotations in priority order, yours and Built Ins alike: higher numbers are tried first, equal priorities by name. It picks the first that matches; a rotation with no switch condition always matches, so turn it off to keep it from being chosen. The fallback (Default) is used only when none matches. The rotation list is sorted in this same order and shows each priority."] = "El cambio automático prueba las rotaciones activadas por orden de prioridad, tanto las tuyas como las integradas: los números más altos se prueban primero y, a igual prioridad, se ordena por nombre. Elige la primera que coincide; una rotación sin condición de cambio siempre coincide, así que desactívala para que no se elija. La rotación de reserva (Predeterminado) solo se usa cuando ninguna coincide. La lista de rotaciones se ordena con este mismo criterio y muestra cada prioridad."
-- en: "A Built In shows a blue Read-Only pill in place of Undo and Redo; Duplicate makes your own copy. It loads only for the edition and class it was written for (the pill's tooltip). The specializations it is for show beside its ID; any level it needs is part of its switch condition. The switch's tooltip says when it can be selected together with another rotation, or is for another specialization."
L["A Built In shows a blue Read-Only pill in place of Undo and Redo; Duplicate makes your own copy. It loads only for the edition and class it was written for (the pill's tooltip). The specializations it is for show beside its ID; any level it needs is part of its switch condition. The switch's tooltip says when it can be selected together with another rotation, or is for another specialization."] = "Una rotación integrada muestra una etiqueta azul de Solo lectura en lugar de Deshacer y Rehacer; Duplicar crea tu propia copia. Solo se carga para la edición y la clase para las que se escribió (la descripción emergente de la etiqueta). Las especializaciones a las que corresponde aparecen junto a su ID; cualquier nivel que necesite forma parte de su condición de cambio. La descripción emergente del interruptor indica cuándo se puede seleccionar junto con otra rotación o si es para otra especialización."
-- en: "In the list, a red border means the rotation cannot be selected (the tooltip names why), gray means it is switched off, and an amber bar means it can be selected at the same time as another rotation (yours or Built In), so only priority decides between them; a wider bar means they also have the same priority and the name decides. /rm why lists the order and what automatic switching would choose now."
L["In the list, a red border means the rotation cannot be selected (the tooltip names why), gray means it is switched off, and an amber bar means it can be selected at the same time as another rotation (yours or Built In), so only priority decides between them; a wider bar means they also have the same priority and the name decides. /rm why lists the order and what automatic switching would choose now."] = "En la lista, un borde rojo significa que la rotación no se puede seleccionar (la descripción emergente indica el motivo), gris significa que está desactivada y una barra ámbar significa que se puede seleccionar a la vez que otra rotación (tuya o integrada), de modo que solo la prioridad decide entre ellas; una barra más ancha significa que además tienen la misma prioridad y decide el nombre. /rm why muestra el orden y lo que elegiría ahora el cambio automático."
-- en: "Same priority as %s: both can be selected at once, and the tie is decided by name."
L["Same priority as %s: both can be selected at once, and the tie is decided by name."] = "Misma prioridad que %s: ambas se pueden seleccionar a la vez y el empate lo decide el nombre."
-- en: "Can be selected together with %s: only priority decides which is chosen."
L["Can be selected together with %s: only priority decides which is chosen."] = "Se puede seleccionar junto con %s: solo la prioridad decide cuál se elige."
-- en: "Loads only for: %s. Its specializations and switch condition decide the rest."
L["Loads only for: %s. Its specializations and switch condition decide the rest."] = "Solo se carga para: %s. Sus especializaciones y su condición de cambio deciden el resto."
-- en: "Each rotation says which specializations it is for, beside its ID: several, or Any. It is listed, in the minimap menu and for /rm set, only while you play one of them; its switch condition never hides it. Automatic switching checks the specialization first, then the switch condition, then priority; a rotation with no switch condition matches whenever its specialization and level apply, so priority alone decides; turn it off to keep it for choosing by hand. The specialization menu above the list's search box starts at the one you are playing; choose another, or All specializations, to see theirs. Where the game has dual specialization instead of named specializations (Classic Era, TBC, Wrath, Cataclysm and Forever), they are your primary and secondary talents: exports leave them out, and an import is for the talents the list shows."
L["Each rotation says which specializations it is for, beside its ID: several, or Any. It is listed, in the minimap menu and for /rm set, only while you play one of them; its switch condition never hides it. Automatic switching checks the specialization first, then the switch condition, then priority; a rotation with no switch condition matches whenever its specialization and level apply, so priority alone decides; turn it off to keep it for choosing by hand. The specialization menu above the list's search box starts at the one you are playing; choose another, or All specializations, to see theirs. Where the game has dual specialization instead of named specializations (Classic Era, TBC, Wrath, Cataclysm and Forever), they are your primary and secondary talents: exports leave them out, and an import is for the talents the list shows."] = "Cada rotación indica a qué especializaciones corresponde, junto a su ID: varias, o Cualquiera. Aparece en la lista, en el menú del minimapa y para /rm set solo mientras juegas con una de ellas; su condición de cambio nunca la oculta. El cambio automático comprueba primero la especialización, luego la condición de cambio y después la prioridad; una rotación sin condición de cambio coincide siempre que se cumplan su especialización y su nivel, así que decide solo la prioridad; desactívala para reservarla para elegirla a mano. El menú de especialización que hay sobre el cuadro de búsqueda de la lista empieza en la que estás jugando; elige otra, o Todas las especializaciones, para ver las suyas. Donde el juego tiene doble especialización en lugar de especializaciones con nombre (Classic Era, TBC, Wrath, Cataclysm y Forever), son tus talentos primarios y secundarios: las exportaciones los omiten y una importación corresponde a los talentos que muestra la lista."
